1
00:00:07,652 --> 00:00:11,723
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:13,358 --> 00:00:15,460
This is a joke!

3
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:17,128
I'm finally heading the
way I'm supposed to,

4
00:00:17,128 --> 00:00:20,665
and somebody's gone and stacked
up a wall of concrete dividers for me.

5
00:00:20,665 --> 00:00:22,300
This is non-negotiable!

6
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,402
I HAVE TO GO THIS WAY!

7
00:00:24,402 --> 00:00:26,571
I've gone down every other passage here.

8
00:00:26,571 --> 00:00:29,807
There hasn't even been a locked door.
Just a straight-up dead end.

9
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:32,277
Christ, they double-stacked it.

10
00:00:32,677 --> 00:00:33,611
I guess I could...

11
00:00:34,412 --> 00:00:35,313
...climb over this.

12
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:38,416
But that kind of defeats the
purpose of killing everybody.

13
00:00:38,416 --> 00:00:41,252
That's why I did it, so I could
have a smooth ride out of here.

14
00:00:41,252 --> 00:00:43,855
I deserve business-class!

15
00:00:43,855 --> 00:00:45,657
Screw this, I'm just going to ram it.

16
00:00:46,858 --> 00:00:48,126
It won't accomplish anything,

17
00:00:48,126 --> 00:00:50,495
but it should derail the train
and that'll look cool.

18
00:00:50,495 --> 00:00:53,498
This reminds me of back in high school
when we had a driver's ed class

19
00:00:53,498 --> 00:00:56,401
and the gym teacher was asking
us which was more dangerous:

20
00:00:56,401 --> 00:00:59,871
Crashing a motorcycle at
60 miles-per-hour into a haystack,

21
00:00:59,871 --> 00:01:03,508
or crashing a motorcycle at
60 miles-per-hour into a concrete divider.

22
00:01:03,508 --> 00:01:06,611
He got mad and started yelling
at the class when no one answered.

23
00:01:06,611 --> 00:01:09,447
Okay, time to end my
tram-operating career.

24
00:01:09,447 --> 00:01:12,250
If I was a conductor, this is
how I would want to retire.

25
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:15,086
Just jump off and let it speed
away with everyone on board.

26
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:17,255
Hey, what the hell?!

27
00:01:17,255 --> 00:01:19,290
That should've stopped a dump truck!

28
00:01:19,791 --> 00:01:22,160
I don't understand anything today.

29
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:25,830
Maybe they were made out of Styrofoam
and just painted to look like concrete.

30
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:29,534
Somebody was just trying to psyche me
out so I wouldn't go this way.

31
00:01:29,534 --> 00:01:30,802
Well, it didn't work!

32
00:01:30,802 --> 00:01:32,737
I made it through anyway!

33
00:01:32,737 --> 00:01:34,739
I'm too clever for that.

34
00:01:34,739 --> 00:01:39,010
Actually, I guess I'm not, because I
really did think it was concrete.

35
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:43,815
But, nobody was around to see me
get confused, so I'm still a genius.

36
00:01:43,815 --> 00:01:45,083
Hey, who are you?

37
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:46,117
What are you doing here?

38
00:01:47,485 --> 00:01:48,553
Give me some money.

39
00:01:48,553 --> 00:01:50,455
GUARD: Freeman, I've
been waiting for you.

40
00:01:50,455 --> 00:01:52,757
GUARD: One of your scientist
pals said to give you a message.

41
00:01:52,757 --> 00:01:53,024
What?

42
00:01:53,024 --> 00:01:54,959
GUARD: You're supposed to
take this old rail system

43
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:58,129
GUARD: up to some kind of
satellite delivery rocket.

44
00:01:58,129 --> 00:01:59,564
GUARD: I don't know where it is exactly,

45
00:01:59,564 --> 00:02:02,100
GUARD: and the old guy was so
worried about getting out of here alive

46
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,201
GUARD: he didn't tell me.

47
00:02:03,201 --> 00:02:06,037
GUARD: Main thing is: the
military aborted the launch.

48
00:02:06,037 --> 00:02:07,972
GUARD: So, when you do find the rocket,

49
00:02:07,972 --> 00:02:10,875
GUARD: you'll have to get up to the
control room and launch it yourself.

50
00:02:10,875 --> 00:02:12,677
GUARD: He said something about a Lambda Team
No, listen, that's not my job!

51
00:02:12,677 --> 00:02:14,946
GUARD: needing the satellite in orbit
No!  Shut up!

52
00:02:14,946 --> 00:02:16,581
GUARD: if they were ever gonna
clean up this mess.

53
00:02:16,581 --> 00:02:18,950
Look, you have the
wrong person, all right?

54
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:21,052
A lot of the scientists here are senile.

55
00:02:21,052 --> 00:02:23,621
They probably said my name or were
thinking about somebody else.

56
00:02:23,621 --> 00:02:24,989
What are you doing?

57
00:02:24,989 --> 00:02:27,959
Well, whatever.  Thanks for
stopping the tram car, I guess.

58
00:02:27,959 --> 00:02:29,594
I'm not sure how you did that.

59
00:02:29,594 --> 00:02:30,428
Hm.

60
00:02:30,428 --> 00:02:31,896
Oh, and there's no exit behind me,

61
00:02:31,896 --> 00:02:33,898
so you're going to die
down here if you don't leave.

62
00:02:34,799 --> 00:02:35,233
Later!

63
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:37,735
Ah!  String things.

64
00:02:38,703 --> 00:02:40,772
Okay, you're dead.

65
00:02:42,173 --> 00:02:43,174
[barnacle gurgles]

66
00:02:43,174 --> 00:02:45,877
God dammit! I did it again!

67
00:02:45,877 --> 00:02:47,545
And we're going down!

68
00:02:47,545 --> 00:02:49,147
This is screwed!

69
00:02:49,147 --> 00:02:51,349
Oh, nice! It's flooded!

70
00:02:51,816 --> 00:02:52,984
Does this even work?

71
00:02:53,718 --> 00:02:55,987
Oh. Hope it lasts.

72
00:02:55,987 --> 00:02:58,656
Can't have the bloodmobile stop now.

73
00:02:58,656 --> 00:03:01,459
God, I am just covered in blood again.

74
00:03:01,459 --> 00:03:04,929
It's too bad I can't duck my
head inside my suit like a turtle.

75
00:03:04,929 --> 00:03:07,632
Then I could just ride by
covered in blood with no head

76
00:03:07,632 --> 00:03:09,434
and people would have to
make up stories about me.

77
00:03:09,834 --> 00:03:12,270
Whoa!  What's that electrical arc there?

78
00:03:12,904 --> 00:03:14,706
Okay, I'm going to go slowly.

79
00:03:16,007 --> 00:03:18,309
Ah-ah!  There it is again.

80
00:03:18,309 --> 00:03:19,677
I'd better pick up the pace.

81
00:03:19,677 --> 00:03:24,048
Electric mystery bolts of death
are...not...my thing.

82
00:03:24,048 --> 00:03:26,317
Thank goodness I'm wearing a metal suit.

83
00:03:26,317 --> 00:03:27,118
[strange yowling noise]

84
00:03:27,118 --> 00:03:28,019
[strange yowling noise]
What's that noise?

85
00:03:28,019 --> 00:03:30,688
[strange yowling noise]

86
00:03:30,688 --> 00:03:31,055
[strange yowling noise]
What?

87
00:03:31,055 --> 00:03:32,957
[strange yowling noise]

88
00:03:32,957 --> 00:03:35,660
All right, I'm not an expert in the field,

89
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:38,663
but that sounds to me like the
cries of the damned.

90
00:03:38,663 --> 00:03:40,465
I'm not where I should be.

91
00:03:41,299 --> 00:03:44,135
I'm going to come across a bunch
of dudes in robes chanting,

92
00:03:44,135 --> 00:03:47,038
making some sort of
sacrifice with daggers.

93
00:03:47,038 --> 00:03:50,041
Then I'm going to have to fight their
summoned demons or whatever.

94
00:03:50,041 --> 00:03:52,143
Hey, maybe that's the--PLAH!

95
00:03:52,143 --> 00:03:54,078
Maybe that's what I've been
dealing with today.

96
00:03:54,078 --> 00:03:57,081
What I've been calling aliens
are really demons.

97
00:03:57,081 --> 00:03:58,816
Not that they can't be both.

98
00:03:58,816 --> 00:04:02,520
Like how every square is a
rectangle but not vice versa.

99
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,689
Hey, are those boards
blocking the track?

100
00:04:04,689 --> 00:04:05,623
[rumbling]

101
00:04:05,623 --> 00:04:07,692
[rumbling]
Oh!  That's a good sign.

102
00:04:07,692 --> 00:04:10,261
Is this thing going to collapse
if I move forward?

103
00:04:10,261 --> 00:04:12,897
Knowing our engineering, this is
made out of balsa wood.

104
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:16,067
Okay....

105
00:04:17,268 --> 00:04:20,638
Oh, that's good.
Playing Jenga with my life.

106
00:04:21,706 --> 00:04:22,974
Crack....

107
00:04:22,974 --> 00:04:25,176
Well, the tunnel hasn't
collapsed yet.

108
00:04:25,176 --> 00:04:28,179
I don't understand how that got
built in the first place.

109
00:04:28,179 --> 00:04:32,450
Why would anyone build a wooden platform
right across the tracks like that?

110
00:04:32,450 --> 00:04:35,653
Maybe some bum has been living down here
and the trains don't get used much,

111
00:04:35,653 --> 00:04:37,655
so he was building his house there.

112
00:04:37,655 --> 00:04:41,092
He was probably planning to jack
the track's current for his own house,

113
00:04:41,092 --> 00:04:43,094
use the water below as a sewer,

114
00:04:43,094 --> 00:04:45,096
and maybe tap into some of the pipes.

115
00:04:45,096 --> 00:04:46,497
That's pretty hardcore.

116
00:04:46,497 --> 00:04:49,834
I don't think I'd have the guts to build
my house in the middle of a train track.

117
00:04:49,834 --> 00:04:50,401
AH!

118
00:04:51,002 --> 00:04:52,136
Who's doing this?

119
00:04:52,136 --> 00:04:55,206
I hope the bum doesn't stalk me
because I played the big, bad wolf

120
00:04:55,206 --> 00:04:57,108
and ran a train through his house.

121
00:04:57,108 --> 00:04:59,277
Oh!  What's this?

122
00:04:59,277 --> 00:05:01,679
Aliens who can't shoot back!

123
00:05:01,679 --> 00:05:03,147
[houndeyes chirp]
I'm going to take my time here.

124
00:05:04,682 --> 00:05:06,150
Come on.  Stand still.

125
00:05:07,852 --> 00:05:08,286
What?

126
00:05:09,053 --> 00:05:10,755
I think that's all of them.

127
00:05:10,755 --> 00:05:12,957
So, are these demons or just aliens?

128
00:05:12,957 --> 00:05:15,159
If they're demons, I could fool them.

129
00:05:15,159 --> 00:05:18,696
I could duck my head inside my suit
to pull off the headless rider act.

130
00:05:18,696 --> 00:05:20,531
I'm already covered in blood.

131
00:05:20,531 --> 00:05:23,034
They would see me pass and
wouldn't think anything of it.

132
00:05:23,034 --> 00:05:24,402
[bullsquid grunting]
Hey, is this the right--AAH!

133
00:05:25,236 --> 00:05:27,138
Christ!  God!  Jesus!

134
00:05:28,339 --> 00:05:30,508
[turret beeping]
Oh, I know that sound!

135
00:05:30,508 --> 00:05:31,676
[turret beeping]
Christ, the fun just

136
00:05:31,676 --> 00:05:33,978
[turret beeping]
doesn't end around here, does it?

137
00:05:33,978 --> 00:05:36,147
[turret beeping]
Bomb shelter parties are the best parties

138
00:05:36,147 --> 00:05:38,883
[turret beeping]
because bomb shelter parties don't stop.

139
00:05:38,883 --> 00:05:40,451
[turret beeping]
Until everyone's dead.

140
00:05:40,451 --> 00:05:41,419
[turret beeping]

141
00:05:41,419 --> 00:05:41,819
[turret firing]

142
00:05:41,819 --> 00:05:42,987
[turret beeping]
There it is.

143
00:05:42,987 --> 00:05:45,089
[turret beeping]
This really isn't worth my time.

144
00:05:45,089 --> 00:05:47,258
[turret beeping]
Stupid sentry gun.

145
00:05:47,258 --> 00:05:48,092
[explosion]

146
00:05:48,092 --> 00:05:50,194
They need to learn I'm their master.

147
00:05:50,194 --> 00:05:52,630
I'm not going to be around
to kill them forever.

148
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:56,100
Okay, what's the deal with this
hook thing blocking the track?

149
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,536
This looks heavy.
I don't want to move it.

150
00:05:58,536 --> 00:06:00,538
I'm sick of all this manual labor!

151
00:06:00,538 --> 00:06:04,008
I am practically royalty!
I shouldn't have to stand for this.

152
00:06:04,008 --> 00:06:05,476
Maybe I could take it on foot.

153
00:06:05,476 --> 00:06:08,579
This train's only saved me about
five minutes of walking anyway.

154
00:06:08,579 --> 00:06:12,183
I'll just go along the ledge--
no, I don't think I want to go this way.

155
00:06:12,183 --> 00:06:14,919
I'll come back once I'm
convinced this is the right way.

156
00:06:14,919 --> 00:06:16,754
I'm not convinced of that at all.

157
00:06:16,754 --> 00:06:17,922
What's this thing?

158
00:06:17,922 --> 00:06:19,023
Maybe I broke it.

159
00:06:19,023 --> 00:06:20,291
That could be--here.

160
00:06:20,925 --> 00:06:23,661
There, it clicked.  I must've fixed it.

161
00:06:23,661 --> 00:06:26,297
I have to fix everything
in this damned building.

162
00:06:27,031 --> 00:06:28,266
This isn't my job.

163
00:06:28,933 --> 00:06:30,968
See, this is what we need slaves for.

164
00:06:30,968 --> 00:06:33,838
I think we really screwed up the
handling of that as a nation.

165
00:06:33,838 --> 00:06:35,673
We were only enslaving black people.

166
00:06:35,673 --> 00:06:38,109
That's stupid.
That's redneck reasoning.

167
00:06:38,109 --> 00:06:41,779
We should've just freed the existing
slaves, wiped the slate clean,

168
00:06:41,779 --> 00:06:43,881
and grabbed new slaves
from a larger pool.

169
00:06:43,881 --> 00:06:45,516
Like, if you play the lottery.

170
00:06:45,516 --> 00:06:46,784
You can win a million dollars,

171
00:06:46,784 --> 00:06:49,420
or you can become a slave for
life if you pick the wrong number.

172
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,856
That's a better risk vs. reward balance.

173
00:06:51,856 --> 00:06:54,492
I mean, what the hell
kind of risk is a $1 ticket?

174
00:06:54,492 --> 00:06:57,428
Do the same thing for voting,
getting a driver's license--

175
00:06:57,428 --> 00:07:01,165
have a new system where every society
member has a small risk to become a slave,

176
00:07:01,165 --> 00:07:02,166
except me.

177
00:07:02,166 --> 00:07:03,367
Especially you!

178
00:07:05,703 --> 00:07:06,437
Hold on.

179
00:07:06,437 --> 00:07:07,772
Stop.  Stop.

180
00:07:07,772 --> 00:07:08,706
Back it up.

181
00:07:08,706 --> 00:07:09,874
This might go somewhere.

182
00:07:12,777 --> 00:07:14,078
Yeah, I'm kidding, of course.

183
00:07:14,078 --> 00:07:17,548
I have serious doubts that you
bastards can even be domesticated.

184
00:07:17,548 --> 00:07:20,084
My soccer ball game was
a much better idea.

185
00:07:20,084 --> 00:07:22,620
Okay, anyone else have a surprise for me?

186
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:22,987
No.

187
00:07:22,987 --> 00:07:24,288
[strange yowling noise]

188
00:07:24,288 --> 00:07:24,722
[strange yowling noise]
Ah.

189
00:07:24,722 --> 00:07:26,891
[strange yowling noise]

190
00:07:26,891 --> 00:07:30,194
Okay, yeah, that either sounds
like a really exotic bird,

191
00:07:30,194 --> 00:07:34,098
or else damned souls crying out to be
released from their never-ending agony.

192
00:07:34,098 --> 00:07:36,534
I can't think of any other options.

193
00:07:36,534 --> 00:07:37,501
What's over here?

194
00:07:39,203 --> 00:07:40,171
Stuff.

195
00:07:40,171 --> 00:07:41,038
[bullsquid grunts]

196
00:07:41,038 --> 00:07:41,639
Gah!

197
00:07:43,007 --> 00:07:44,475
Wow, I guess it should've occurred to me

198
00:07:44,475 --> 00:07:47,211
that there's a reason this room
is full of dead bodies.

199
00:07:47,211 --> 00:07:48,646
I walked into that one.

200
00:07:48,646 --> 00:07:50,114
Hey, ammo.

201
00:07:50,114 --> 00:07:51,482
Hm.  I don't have a bandolier.

202
00:07:51,482 --> 00:07:53,851
Maybe I should make a necklace
out of the extra clips.

203
00:07:53,851 --> 00:07:56,921
I bet I'm one of the few people
who has need of a bandolier.

204
00:07:58,122 --> 00:07:59,123
Gotcha, bug.

205
00:08:01,225 --> 00:08:02,760
Oh, wow!  It opened.

206
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,228
Something must be wrong.

207
00:08:04,228 --> 00:08:06,097
[headcrab squeals, HECU groans]

208
00:08:06,097 --> 00:08:08,466
Yeah, I don't think this is the right way.

209
00:08:08,466 --> 00:08:10,768
And you look busy, I'll leave
you to your work.

210
00:08:10,768 --> 00:08:11,869
Don't follow me!

211
00:08:11,869 --> 00:08:13,237
Don't follow me.

212
00:08:13,237 --> 00:08:14,605
I don't take strays.

213
00:08:14,605 --> 00:08:17,208
[shotgun blasts]

214
00:08:17,208 --> 00:08:19,944
Yeah, see, it sounds like you
have everything under control.

215
00:08:19,944 --> 00:08:22,313
I mean, if they don't kill you,
then I have to shoot you myself,

216
00:08:22,313 --> 00:08:23,881
and that's just more work for me.

217
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:28,119
Case in point!

218
00:08:28,119 --> 00:08:30,054
You know what the ridiculous
thing about all of this--

219
00:08:30,054 --> 00:08:31,322
[bullsquid spits]

220
00:08:31,322 --> 00:08:32,323
[bullsquid moans]

221
00:08:32,323 --> 00:08:34,725
The ridiculous thing is--hey, a switch.

222
00:08:35,793 --> 00:08:37,495
...is not only did he choose
this line of work,

223
00:08:37,495 --> 00:08:40,231
but he's probably getting paid
pretty well for this, with hazard pay.

224
00:08:40,231 --> 00:08:43,701
Meanwhile, I'm caught in the middle of
this and I'm not getting paid anything.

225
00:08:43,701 --> 00:08:46,137
I'm basically doing volunteer
work right now.

226
00:08:46,137 --> 00:08:47,672
These are community service hours.

227
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,809
God DAMN that is nasty.

228
00:08:53,077 --> 00:08:53,644
Ugh.

229
00:08:54,278 --> 00:08:57,648
See, I don't want to be here,
but somebody has to kill everything.

230
00:08:57,648 --> 00:08:59,784
I am not getting used to this.

231
00:09:02,286 --> 00:09:06,991
Oh my....eugh....

232
00:09:06,991 --> 00:09:08,292
I've gotta get out of here.

233
00:09:08,292 --> 00:09:11,462
This is like a repeat of when I
worked in fast food that summer.

234
00:09:11,462 --> 00:09:12,997
Oh!  God!

235
00:09:12,997 --> 00:09:14,899
Well, I guess this
part's a little different.

236
00:09:14,899 --> 00:09:18,102
I mean, we would joke about
mystery meat, but look at this.

237
00:09:18,102 --> 00:09:20,738
Okay, elevator, good...

238
00:09:20,738 --> 00:09:22,239
Sparks, bad...

239
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,008
Damn, damn, DAMMIT!

240
00:09:24,842 --> 00:09:27,044
QUIT BEING METAL!

241
00:09:29,547 --> 00:09:31,547
If I was a wizard,
this wouldn't be happening.

